  "notes": "Geometry enters only through the NURBS description; the native meshes contribute cell-centre positions alone, as query points and as volume anchor positions. Every native cell is decoded directly, so every mapping is the identity with coverage 1.0 and no interpolation, nearest-neighbour assignment or extrapolation is applied. Surface and volume queries are decoded in chunks of 2000000, the last chunk of each holding the remainder; each forward pass decodes one surface chunk and one volume chunk against the same geometry and anchor context, recomputed from identical inputs, and query points are never attention keys, so chunking changes nothing beyond the run-to-run GPU rounding differences described in the method record. Training counts are over the 400 training cases and inference counts over the 50 test cases."
